# Coldline - Task 4.10
# File: .gitignore
# Component: Repository hygiene
# Purpose: Exclude local tools, caches, runtime state, OpenTofu state, and generated security evidence from commits.
# Interacts With: Git and local development tools, poe security-scan, the Task 6 evidence tools, poe tofu-plan, poe tofu-apply, poe tofu-destroy, poe verify
# Sprint/Task: Sprint 4 - Project 4 / Task 4.10
# Concepts: Clean working tree, generated files never in a Task diff
# Tools: Git

.env
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tools/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Optional captures describe this checkpoint; they are not submission artifacts.
.benchmark/

# Task 4.5: the scan report and the software bill of materials `poe security-scan` writes,
# and the evidence files the Task 6 tools will write. Generated on every run, uploaded by
# the security-gate job as a workflow artifact, never part of a Task diff.
reports/
evidence/

# Add-On 4.10: what OpenTofu writes beside your declarations: the provider directory, the
# state file and its backup, the lock-info file during a run, and any saved plan. Your
# sandbox's state stays on your computer and never enters a pull request. `poe verify` keeps
# its own working copy and state under .tools/tofu-verify/, and the provider cache under
# .tools/tofu-plugins/, both ignored with .tools/ above.
infra/tofu/.terraform/
*.tfstate*
*.tfplan
crash.log
